.TH LN 1
.SH NAME
ln \- link a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ln
.I from to
.br
.B ln \-s
.I target path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ln
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It gives the existing file
.I from
a second name,
.I to
(a hard link: both names are the same file).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s
A symbolic link instead:
.I path
holds the text
.IR target ,
which need not exist; it is followed when
.I path
is opened.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR mv (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
Hard links do not cross volumes.
